WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.527
Accountability reform history.

00:00:02.477 --> 00:00:04.500
Every attempt blocked.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:13.250
This page documents every major accountability reform proposed in Canadian history and shows how the captured system blocked, weakened, or neutered each one.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:21.056
The Federal Accountability Act of 2006 was the most ambitious reform attempt — and was systematically weakened during implementation.

00:00:21.056 --> 00:00:25.068
ATIP reform has been proposed for decades and remains inadequate.

00:00:25.068 --> 00:00:29.363
Senate reform requires constitutional amendment that will never happen.

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:33.352
Ethics enforcement was designed with penalties too weak to deter.

00:00:33.352 --> 00:00:37.795
Whistleblower protection was written to protect the system, not the whistleblower.

00:00:37.795 --> 00:00:40.988
Each reform was proposed with good intentions.

00:00:40.988 --> 00:00:47.374
Each was blocked by the institutional architecture documented across two hundred and sixty-three pages on this site.

00:00:47.374 --> 00:00:53.772
The history of accountability reform in Canada is the history of captured institutions preventing their own reform.

00:00:53.772 --> 00:00:55.852
The reform timeline.

00:00:55.852 --> 00:00:59.840
Each entry documents a reform attempt and how it was blocked.
